.TH LLMCPP-AGENT 1 "" "llmcpp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llmcpp-agent \- provide an external LLM backend for llmc++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llmcpp-agent
.br
.B llmcpp-agent \-\-replay
.I transcript
.br
.B llmcpp-agent \-\-mcp\-bridge
.I socket
.SH DESCRIPTION
llmcpp-agent is the bundled Python adapter for llmc++. The compiler normally
launches it; it is not an interactive prompt interface.
.PP
It exchanges newline-delimited JSON-RPC over standard input and output.
It initializes an MCP client connection, discovers compiler tools, and
handles protocol-version-1 llm/generate requests. It uses compiler tools to
inspect context, validate candidate bodies, and submit accepted code.
Diagnostics go to standard error; standard output is reserved for protocol
messages.
.PP
The adapter supports the Anthropic API, OpenAI Responses API, Codex CLI,
and Claude Code CLI.
Codex and Claude Code require installed, authenticated CLI tools.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the llmcpp-agent version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " transcript"
Replay recorded tool calls from an llmc++ JSONL transcript without contacting
a model. The compiler still validates submitted bodies.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-bridge " socket"
Run the internal MCP bridge used by CLI backends. Connect to the specified
Unix-domain socket. This mode is normally started by the adapter itself.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Supply a JSON object through llmc++ \-fllm\-agent\-config=file.
Supported fields are model, effort, executable, base_url, and api_key.
Only fields relevant to the selected backend apply.
.PP
Configuration values override environment defaults. A model requested by the
compiler, including a per-function model override, takes precedence over
the configuration model. Prefer environment variables for credentials.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLMCPP_BACKEND
Select anthropic, openai, codex, or claude. Required unless replaying
a transcript.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API credential for the Anthropic backend.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
Override the Anthropic API endpoint.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API credential for the OpenAI backend.
.TP
.B OPENAI_BASE_URL
Override the OpenAI API endpoint. Defaults to https://api.openai.com.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_MODEL
Model identifier or alias. API defaults are claude-opus-5 for Anthropic
and gpt-6-astra for OpenAI;
CLI backends otherwise use their own defaults.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_EFFORT
Reasoning effort for Codex and Claude Code. Default: medium.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_CODEX
Codex executable name or path. Default: codex.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_CLAUDE
Claude Code executable name or path. Default: claude.
.TP
.B LLMCPP_VERBOSE
Enable diagnostics with 1, true, yes, or on. Disable with 0, false, no, or off.
Also set by llmc++ \-fllm\-verbose.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
LLMCPP_BACKEND=codex llmc++ main.cpp \-o main
llmc++ \-fllm\-backend=openai \-fllm\-agent=llmcpp-agent main.cpp
llmc++ \-fllm\-agent='llmcpp-agent \-\-replay trace.jsonl' main.cpp
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Normal protocol completion returns zero. Generation errors are reported in
JSON-RPC results and need not terminate the process. Unexpected process
failures may return a nonzero status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llmc++ (1),
.BR python3 (1)
